<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="sec-2-10-moving-on" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Moving On!</title>

  <p>
    Congratulations!
  </p>

  <p>
    In this chapter, you have learned the entire foundation of procedural Java programming:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <p>How Java applications are structured into classes and methods.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>How data is stored in memory using primitive types, variables, and constants.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>How to evaluate mathematical expressions with arithmetic operators and the <c>Math</c> library while avoiding finite binary pitfalls.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>How text objects behave in the heap, and why strings are immutable.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>How to format output using <c>print</c>, <c>println</c>, and <c>printf</c>.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>How to gather interactive keyboard input with <c>Scanner</c>.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>How to apply a structured, five-step engineering process to solve complete problems and verify them with tests and the debugger.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    You are now fully equipped to tackle the programming exercises at the end of this chapter. Work through the steps: explore the problem on paper, design your algorithm, prepare your test cases, build incrementally, verify your results, and take pride in your new and hard-earned abilities!
  </p>
</section>
